        <div id="amazon" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Can You Buy Trader Joe's Protein Powder on Amazon?
          </h2>

          <p>
            No. Trader Joe's does not sell online, and it does not sell its products on Amazon. Any Trader Joe's item you see on Amazon or eBay is from a third-party reseller, usually at a large markup and with no guarantee of how it was stored. We found a Trader Joe's collagen listing on one reseller site at many times the $7.99 store price, which is a good reason to avoid them.
          </p>

          <p>
            The good news is that the main product Trader Joe's stocks is easy to replace. Orgain's regular Organic Protein is on Amazon with the same 21 g of protein per serving, and at the $31.98 we saw for the 2.03 lb tub it costs about $1.90 per 25 g, close to the Trader Joe's price. It is sweetened with stevia rather than a cane sugar blend, so it may taste slightly different.
          </p>

          <p>
            For readers who were really after Trader Joe's old house whey or plain pea powder, the better Amazon swaps are bulk bags. Nutricost Whey Protein Concentrate gives 25 g of protein per scoop at about $1.42 per 25 g, and NOW Sports Pea Protein gives 24 g per scoop at about $0.73 per 25 g, both at the prices we saw. Plant-protein shoppers comparing newer brands may also want our sibling review of <a href="/kos-protein-powder-review/">KOS protein powder</a>, another organic plant blend sold widely in grocery stores, and the <a href="/best-pea-protein-powder/">best pea protein powder</a> rankings.
          </p>

          <p>
            Who should still buy at Trader Joe's? Occasional users who want one small tub for smoothies, people avoiding dairy, and anyone who values organic ingredients over price per gram. Daily shake drinkers, lifters and drug-tested athletes will be better served elsewhere, by a store-brand whey for value or a certified powder for testing. For the full list of low-cost options, start with our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">best cheap protein powder</a> guide, or compare specific products on our <a href="/compare/">comparison pages</a>.
          </p>
