          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming Trader Joe's still stocks its house whey</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Older articles and calorie apps still list Trader Joe's Whey Protein Powder, but we could not find it on the Trader Joe's website today. Ask a crew member before making a special trip, and have a backup plan such as Aldi's Elevation or Costco's Kirkland whey if the tub turns out to be gone.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Counting collagen as a complete protein</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Trader Joe's own product page says its Hydrolyzed Collagen does not meet the FDA standard for a whole protein because it lacks tryptophan. It is a useful 11 g coffee add-in, but it should not replace a whey or pea powder as your main protein source if muscle is the goal.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Judging value by the shelf price alone</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $14.99 tub sounds cheap until you divide by protein. At about 10 servings of 21 g, the Trader Joe's Orgain tub costs around $1.78 per 25 g, more than double Kirkland whey. Always work out the cost per 25 g of protein before you decide something is a bargain.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating USDA Organic as proof of purity</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The Orgain tub's organic seal covers how the peas and other crops were grown, not testing for heavy metals or banned substances. Trader Joe's and Orgain publish no sport certification for these powders, so drug-tested athletes should buy an NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport product instead.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying reseller prices for Trader Joe's items online</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Trader Joe's does not sell online or on Amazon, so any listing you find there is a third-party reseller charging a markup on a product of unknown age. If you cannot get to a store, order Orgain's regular tub or a bulk whey or pea bag direct from Amazon instead.
              </p>
            </div>
