          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Trader Joe's protein powder third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  No third-party testing is published for the protein powders Trader Joe's sells. The Orgain Protein Boost tub is USDA Organic, but neither Trader Joe's nor Orgain lists NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Sport or a similar certification for it, and the Hydrolyzed Collagen page mentions none either. Drug-tested athletes should choose a certified powder from another retailer.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Trader Joe's protein powder healthy?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The Orgain tub Trader Joe's sells is a reasonable choice: 21 g of organic plant protein per serving and about 130 to 140 calories, per Trader Joe's listing. It does contain added sweeteners, cane sugar and stevia, so check the sugar line on the tub. People with kidney disease, pregnancy or medication should ask a doctor or registered dietitian first.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Trader Joe's sell whey protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Not that we could confirm today. Trader Joe's once sold its own whey in vanilla and chocolate, about $12.99 for 16 oz with 16 g of protein per serving per a 2022 report, but it is not on the current website. Some stores may still have stock. Costco, Aldi, Walmart and Target all sell their own whey.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Trader Joe's protein powder contain dairy or lactose?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The Orgain Organic Protein Boost that Trader Joe's lists is plant-based, built on pea protein, so it contains no whey, casein or lactose. The Hydrolyzed Collagen is made from beef collagen, also dairy-free but not vegan. If Trader Joe's older whey turns up in your store, it is milk-based and contains lactose.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which Trader Joe's protein powder flavor is best?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  We have not tasted them, and Trader Joe's-specific reviews are scarce. On Orgain's widely reviewed listings elsewhere, buyers tend to favor creamy chocolate fudge for drinking in milk or water and use vanilla bean as a smoothie base. Both are the same price at Trader Joe's, so start with whichever suits how you will use it.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the common complaints about Trader Joe's protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The most common complaints are availability and texture. Shoppers on Trader Joe's Reviews were upset when the unsweetened pea powder was discontinued in 2022, and some described it as chalky or bland. With plant powders like Orgain, buyers often mention a gritty texture and a stevia aftertaste, and the small tubs run out quickly for daily users.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is protein powder cheaper at Trader Joe's or Costco?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Costco is far cheaper per gram. Kirkland Signature whey costs roughly $0.70 per 25 g of protein at the warehouse prices we have tracked, against about $1.78 for the Orgain tub at Trader Joe's. Aldi's Elevation whey, at about $0.80 to $0.95 per 25 g, also beats Trader Joe's by a wide margin.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

